---
// The type a notice is read in (docs/spec/notice-modals.md N12), for the two direct pages and
// for the modal over the shelf, so the one text is drawn alike in both.
//
// An Astro scoped style cannot reach text that arrives through a slot, so the rules below go
// through `:global()` under this component's own class. That also lifts them above a host
// page's global rules: `.notice-body :global(p)` is 0,2,1 where `NoticePage`'s old
// `body.notice p` was 0,1,2. The shelf page's own global `h1` reaches the modal's heading too,
// so every property it sets is declared here as well, and nothing is left to it.
//
// Markup and styles only: the sizes and colours are what `smoke-render`'s notice cell reads
// (18px, 7:1), and this file is where they live.
---

<div class="notice-body"><slot /></div>

<style>
  .notice-body {
    color: #c9b8a4;
    font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .notice-body :global(h1) {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    color: #f2e8dc;
    font-family:
      'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Mono', 'Segoe UI Mono', 'Roboto Mono', monospace;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .notice-body :global(h2) {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.25rem;
    color: #e0d2c0;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: normal;
  }

  .notice-body :global(p) {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #c9b8a4;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .notice-body :global(a) {
    color: #e8dccd;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }

  .notice-body :global(a:hover),
  .notice-body :global(a:focus-visible) {
    color: #fff4e6;
  }
</style>
